An unordered, forward-facing backlog; completed work and its rationale
live in the git history of this file, docs/plans/, docs/design/, and
NEWS.

Items are listed alphabetically by plan name; the order carries no
meaning. Most items have an implementation plan in docs/plans/<name>.md
(a few record instead in a design doc or a differently-named plan,
named in the item), and the planning/implementation/review process (who
plans, who implements, who reviews, which gates run) is
docs/plans/README.md.
No item is deferred to post-release, and gate labels (decision-gated,
consumer-gated) rank priority rather than block work (VD 2026-07-17).

Standing fact (VD, 2026-07-06): single-chain n >= 1e5 workloads are
common. The large-n performance items are live, not consumer-gated.

items
  bcf-sigma-tail-mixing: OPTIONAL research door (docs/plans/bcf-sigma-
    residual.md sec 4 item 2; no separate plan doc). The BCF sigma SBC
    flag was diagnosed as a slow forest-mixing burn transient and fixed
    for acceptance by pinning absolute burn sweeps (no engine or
    draw-law change). Open: the EXTREME tail (|a0| >= ~40, ~3% of the
    prior) is frozen-structure mixing that no amount of burn fixes; a
    principled remedy would target tree-structure mixing at high SNR
    (tempered early sweeps, restart-style grow proposals). Low priority
    - the regime only arises with a stale build scale swapped against a
    new response inside a larger Gibbs loop (setResponse
    updateScale=FALSE). research-open, decision-gated.
  blocked-jacobi-trees: RESEARCHED, KILLED 2026-07-21 (recorded door;
    docs/plans/blocked-jacobi-trees.md). Noise-splitting augmentation
    for exact parallel tree updates is PROVEN EXACT with only a mild
    per-sweep ESS tax - banked as reusable knowledge - but it is
    memory-bandwidth-bound (~2x serial's traffic in pseudo-response
    scratch), so it loses on x86/DDR4 and, where it wins, is dominated
    by plain within-chain threading, itself NO-GO on the real engine
    (~1.1x, capped by the ~47% parallel fraction; docs/design/within-
    chain-threading.md). Both single-chain-parallelism mechanisms are
    dead; multi-chain remains the way to use cores. Lesson: gate
    threading claims on in-situ real-engine timing, never a kernel
    microbench. Reopen only for a concrete embedded-Gibbs consumer on
    high-bandwidth hardware, or if a fused no-scratch kernel is
    measured to clear the bar on x86 first.
  correlated-outcomes: richer error/outcome covariance around a BART
    mean, delivered via outer-sampler composition (stan4bart = WALNUTS
    + dbarts supplying each outcome's conditional mean; the pattern
    bairrtt uses). RESOLVED 2026-07-22 (docs/design/correlated-
    outcomes.md): (b) multivariate / multiple correlated outcomes
    SHIPPED as mvbart() in stan4bart (e27a7c3) with zero dbarts code -
    SUR chained conditionals reduce each outcome's step to a
    per-observation offset + scalar sd against resid.prior=fixed()
    (mediation is the triangular case, rho the sensitivity knob). What
    remains open: (a) AR-1 / serially-correlated errors (longitudinal,
    panel, ITS, DiD - the Bertrand-Duflo-Mullainathan SE problem)
    compose today via a latent AR-state + nugget in the outer sampler
    (the rbart_vi pattern, AR replacing the intercept), with EXACT
    pure-AR-1 errors a deferred ENGINE door (banded residual precision
    + cross-leaf GLS leaf updates break per-leaf independence).
    Exposing the per-sweep callback on dbartsSampler$run is a perf-only
    convenience, not a gate (demoted in the design doc).
    causal-motivated, decision-gated.
  forest-ranef-interweaving: RESEARCHED, NO-GO now (recorded door;
    docs/design/forest-ranef-interweaving.md). The weak-signal/small-K
    grouped-mixing bottleneck is forest-ranef confounding (several-fold
    and estimator-unstable; permanent gate benchmarks/R/grouped-
    mixing.R). No cheap ASIS exists - the forest exposes no per-group
    knob - and the only real fix, a coupled-leaf collapse
    (marginalize b via per-group Woodbury), couples the constant-leaf
    suffstat across groups/trees on the hot path (~800-1300 lines,
    draw-changing) for a narrow-corner win with a trivial
    longer/parallel-chain workaround. Reopen with VD sign-off for a
    concrete weak-signal/few-groups application needing calibrated tau
    intervals. Secondary: ASIS on (tau, b) is cheap but funnel-only and
    can WORSEN small-K - conditional-go behind a full-engine prototype.
    decision-gated.
  gp-followups: sampled lengthscales (theta prior, per-sample channels,
    real cost - not the mechanical follow-up the proposal suggested);
    low-rank kernels. decision/consumer-gated.
  gpu-bart: backend-seam design waits on frontier items 4-5
    (informed-kernel + CG-leaf prototypes); memo and falsifiers in
    docs/design/gpu-bart.md and parallel-bart-frontier.md.
  group-by-exposure: public group.by beyond rbart_vi
    (grouped-random-effects.md; naming reserved). decision-gated.
  grouped-equivalence: equivalence scenario for grouped rbart_vi fits,
    only if a grouped refactor is planned.
  grow-from-root: frontier 3.1's exact informed-proposal use of the
    shared scan.
  interaction-constraints: deliverable B (per-path max-order + hard
    co-occurrence) and P4 (per-tree block-additive blocks(), plus the
    F1 columnMask warm-start fix) both LANDED 2026-07-21 - f455d7c,
    aadbbc8/103dbe2/073d3db; records in docs/design/interaction-
    constraints.md and the two plan docs. Remaining doors: soft
    path-dependent penalties, formal heredity (ensemble lattice prior)
    - both decision/consumer-gated.
  negbin-real-dispersion: recorded door out of the negative-binomial
    landing (docs/plans/negative-binomial.md; design sec 2 carries fork
    B's spec). Real-valued dispersion needs a non-integer-shape
    Polya-Gamma draw, for which no exact sampler exists, so shipping it
    means dbarts' first documented-approximate family (truncated
    gamma-sum, bias bounded ~1e-3 at K = 200) behind an explicit
    opt-in; the same decision gates weighted-binary's fractional
    weights. The engine seams (shape-parameterized PG helper, r-update
    strategy) are already in place. Poisson family and grouped NB are
    companion doors (design sec 7). decision-gated.
  python-bindings: post kernel-cleanups the engine is R-free below the
    bridge, so a pybind11 facade wrapper is prototype-scale. Horizon,
    likely out-of-repo. Two contracts a non-R host would have to take
    over (2026-07-17 data review): host-side ingestion validation (CSC
    structure, categorical bounds, sparse metadata assembly) lives in
    the R bridge and would need an R-free bartcore ingest helper, and
    mixed/CSC stores hold lifetime borrows anchored by R protection.
    decision-gated.
  repo-modernization: standing hygiene bundle. Open: optional roxygen2
    and NEWS.md migrations (do not start unasked).
  multinomial-level-centering: engine-correctness door out of the SBC
    arc - all three raw per-forest f_ik cells rank U-shaped (chisqP
    0.000) at both chain-length points with lag-9-clean ACF, so mixing
    does not explain it; identified softmax probabilities PASS at both
    points. Memo recorded 2026-08-05: the defect is the draw's MEAN
    (it wipes the whole level every sweep, pinning it ~10x too tight;
    the precision error nearly cancels at the SBC config), it is not
    inert but leaks only second order, and the uniform-absorption
    exact conditional fixes it - validated by a counterfactual SBC
    run (raw f cells clear the band, softmax unchanged). Unanimous
    FIX recommendation across two blind derivations + adversarial
    critique; VD signs off fix vs document
    (docs/plans/multinomial-level-centering.md Memo).
  sbc-family-tiers: BUILT d094675 (2026-08-04) - t and multinomial
    softmax ALL PASS, ordinal 9/10 with gamma3 resolved as ridge
    mixing by the 3x ladder, nbinom identified mu PASS with r/agg.psi
    H-MIX (ESS a few dozen at thin=30; full-R ladder commands recorded
    in the plan). Open doors: raw-f_ik (own item above), the monotone
    follow-on arm (enabler 173a710), the heteroscedastic setState
    lift, full-R ladder re-runs, runSbcBCF repair (diagnosed
    2026-08-05: engine-side, decision-gated - the 9030d93 multi-forest
    mutation guard refuses its anchor-reuse pattern and BCF's
    y-derived leaf-scale calibration blocks rebuild-per-rep; the
    2026-08-05 survey addendum revises the fork: FIX-A needs the
    whole calibration pinned, FIX-B is cheaper than first read and
    has a verified consumer constituency;
    docs/plans/runsbcbcf-repair.md).
  multiforest-mutation-gaps: found by the 2026-08-05 survey -
    setModel unguarded at numForests >= 2 rewrites forest 0 only,
    silently discarding BCF's calibrated mu leaf scale (correctness
    gap, wants a guard or a real path); setOffset/setTreatment are
    silent no-ops on multinomial (should refuse or work)
    (docs/plans/runsbcbcf-repair.md Survey addendum).
  setpredictor-leafof-rebuild: memo recorded 2026-08-05 - the leafOf
    rebuild is only ~21% of the regression (79% is the mu[leafOf]
    gather that replaced contiguous SIMD passes) and the measured
    ceiling of every leafOf-scoped mechanism is +9.7%, still outside
    the gate; decision pending VD: close, or scope a bitwise-safe
    mu[leafOf] gather SIMD item instead
    (docs/plans/setpredictor-leafof-rebuild.md Memo).
  sparse-extensions: streaming range kernel, mutation on dense-backed
    mixed columns, and the smaller deferred extensions in
    docs/plans/sparse-extensions.md's Status list (sparse x.test,
    setData on a CSC store, ...). consumer-gated.
  survival-followups: doors out of the survival family pair (AFT +
    discrete-time hazard both landed; records in docs/plans/survival-
    models.md and docs/design/survival.md sec 6): cloglog link (needs a
    cloglog binary family first), competing risks (crisk.bart's
    territory), left truncation, grouped frailty, time-varying
    covariates in the auto-expander (available today via the manual
    person-period fit), continuous-time models. Each independent;
    demand-driven. low-ranked.
  weighted-binary: post 1.0 - integer-weight probit via replicated
    latents; arbitrary real weights need a real-shape PG sampler (IPW
    is a pseudo-likelihood trap).
  x86-simd: SIMD is closed as a perf lever - compute width is already
    there (the manual unroll plus the per-file -m flag emits 256-bit at
    -O2, measured on the bench box, docs/plans/simd-flag-
    multiversioning.md), and both remaining candidates measured NO-GO:
    NT stores (the fits compaction left no hot store-bound elementwise
    caller, so the commented bodies were deleted; git history keeps
    them) and the SSR SIMD leaf (~0.1% of a sweep, so <=0.05%
    end-to-end, against a permanent cross-ISA fixed-lane/no-FMA
    obligation; docs/design/memory-wall-frontier.md sec 6). The
    windows-arm64 NEON config is validated end-to-end by the
    windows-11-arm CI job in check-standard.yaml (native compile +
    bitwise scalar-vs-NEON; the MSVC intrinsic branch stays unexercised
    by design - R packages build with the Rtools toolchain). The live
    perf frontier past SIMD is the MEMORY WALL: re-profile + census run
    2026-08-04 on dbarts-bench (memory-wall-frontier.md sec 10) - the
    suffstat gather is 46-49% of a sweep, the flagship histogram-fused
    suffstat's premise SURVIVES (ceiling ~1.67x; block-fusion Stage A's
    bench-neutral result is the standing counter-evidence), Z-order /
    locality reordering measured DEAD, data-layout.md re-evaluated and
    closed shelved. Next action: VD fork on building the fused-kernel
    falsifier (measured in situ, never a microbench alone).
    decision-gated.

release (deferred; the one ordered procedure, run when VD triggers it)
  note: the schedule/dispatch-only workflows (equivalence, rchk,
    revdep-smoke, sbc, valgrind) cannot register or run until they
    exist on the default branch - GitHub binds BOTH schedule and
    workflow_dispatch to it, so today they 404 even for a manual run.
    Their first live runs happen when bartcore merges to main;
    validate them then. rchk and valgrind have never run anywhere:
    macOS arm64 supports neither, so the merge is what buys the
    PROTECT-balance and memcheck passes CRAN itself runs. HELD
    2026-07-25 (VD): main stays as it is until VD's own review of the
    branch; revisit these checks then.
  push dbarts 1.0-0 (branch bartcore) and stan4bart 0.0-13; submit both
    to CRAN together. bartCause is ready on branch dbarts-1.0 in
    ~/Repositories/bartCause (two commits, unpushed, checks Status OK):
    push and submit it after dbarts is accepted.
  close GitHub issue #80 at release: fully resolved by the setResponse
    updateScale switch (cf70fd5; default FALSE locks the creation-time
    prior scale - the safe embedded-Gibbs behavior the issue asks for;
    latent families never rescale by construction). Audited 2026-07-18:
    engine behavior spot-checked, dbartsSampler-class.Rd documents the
    default, NEWS 1.0-0 UPGRADING carries the bullet. Point the
    reporter at the Rd and NEWS entries.
  on any post-release dbarts.h change: bump DBARTS_C_API_MINOR (or MAJOR
    if incompatible) alongside the hash re-bake, and bump stan4bart's
    Depends/LinkingTo dbarts floor in the same lockstep release - the
    load handshake covers the library-ahead direction, the floor covers
    consumer-ahead; both must move together.
  optional courtesy: notify the tmle maintainers. Their default
    SuperLearner dbarts wrappers pass obsWeights unconditionally and
    pnorm() the latents; unit weights are handled dbarts-side now, but
    genuinely weighted binomial analyses lose the dbarts learners by
    design, and family routing on their side would need the matching
    inverse link.

